-- title:
--   Freeness of the H-action at affine places of the Drinfeld curve
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$ (the field of $q^2$ elements), and assume the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k` — the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ (polynomials in `Fin 2` variables) by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1` — is a domain; `drinfeldFunctionField q k` is its fraction field. Let $p$ be an element of `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of the character sending $(g,c) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$ to $\det(g)\cdot c^{q+1}$ (the determinant being pushed into $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$), and write $(g,c)$ for its two components; assume $c^2 = 1$ in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. Let $w$ be a place of `drinfeldFunctionField q k` over $k$, that is, a valuation subring containing the image of $k$, not equal to the whole field, and a principal ideal ring. Assume the images of `x q k` and `y q k` in the function field both lie in this valuation subring, and that the ring homomorphism underlying the $k$-algebra automorphism `hFunctionFieldAction q k p` pulls the valuation subring back to itself. Then there is $\varepsilon \in \mathbb{Z}/q$ with $\varepsilon^2 = 1$, $g = \varepsilon \cdot 1$ as a $2 \times 2$ matrix over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and $c$ the image of $\varepsilon$ under $\mathbb{Z}/q \to \mathbb{F}_{q^2}$.
--
--   This is the freeness, up to the scalars $\pm 1$, of the action of the group $H \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q) \times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$ on the affine points of the Drinfeld curve: an element with scalar part of square $1$ fixing a place at which both coordinates are regular must be a scalar. It is used in the analysis of the supersingular components of modular curves of full level, where the non-end points of the prolongation are characterised by the existence of a level automorphism moving them.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_exists_eq_smul_one_of_comap_hFunctionFieldAction_eq_of_affine_of_sq_eq_one.lean

